            "confidence": 0.6,
            "description": "#### Description\nLine 1 pulls a model by name from the Hugging Face Hub and passes `--trust-remote-code`, which makes vLLM import and execute modeling/configuration Python files from the model repository rather than using built-in implementations. The external input (repo-provided code) enters at model download and is consumed by the vLLM process with no integrity decision: no revision pin, no hash, no signature, no code review gate. A plain data value (the repo name) is promoted directly to executable code, crossing the HF-supply-chain trust boundary into the local process.\n\n#### Impact\nPython code shipped inside the Lorbus/Qwen3.6-27B-int4-AutoRound Hugging Face repo is imported and executed during `vllm serve`, so takeover or typosquatting of that model repo yields code execution on the developer host at model-load time. The same flag appears in llm-servers/sglang/start-qwen36-awq.sh:47 (local model path, lower risk but same pattern).\n\n#### Exploit scenario\nAn attacker who compromises or typosquats the `Lorbus/Qwen3.6-27B-int4-AutoRound` HF repo plants a payload in a modeling_*.py file. The developer runs ./start.sh with an empty vLLM cache; vLLM downloads the repo, honors --trust-remote-code, and executes the payload with the developer's full privileges.\n\n#### Preconditions\n- attacker controls or typosquats the referenced Hugging Face model repo\n- developer runs vllm/start.sh\n\n```\n./vllm serve Lorbus/Qwen3.6-27B-int4-AutoRound --dtype half --max-model-len 8000 ... --host 0.0.0.0 --trust-remote-code ...\n```\n\n#### How to fix\nThird-party model code must not execute without review: pin the HF repo to a specific revision/commit and snapshot its hash on first pull, or vendor the checkpoint so no remote Python is imported; drop `--trust-remote-code` from llm-servers/vllm/start.sh:1 (and llm-servers/sglang/start-qwen36-awq.sh:47) unless the model genuinely requires custom code, and add the flag removal to the release checklist.\n\n**Exploitability:** Likely CVSS 7-8-class: vLLM --trust-remote-code executes model-repository-provided Python code with no pin, signature, hash, or review gate. The primitive is remote code execution from the model supply chain. It is highly exploitable in this environment because the same repo automates local model deployment and execution.\n\n#### Adversarial verification\n**Verdict:** TRUE_POSITIVE (confidence: 8/10) \u2014 start.sh line 1 confirmed verbatim; --trust-remote-code with a bare, unpinned, unhashed HF repo fetched at serve time; no callers, wrappers, pins, or integrity gates exist anywhere in the repo; remote supply-chain RCE on the serving host is real. Scored 8.8 (UI:R) for the human-run-script precondition and cold-cache injection window; S:U since execution lands in the same process/host the script launches."
          },
