          "properties": {
            "severity": "medium",
            "security-severity": "5.4",
            "cvssRating": "Medium",
            "category": "CWE-73: External Control of File Name or Path",
            "cvssVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:R/S:C/C:N/I:L/A:L",
            "cwe": "CWE-73 - External Control of File Name or Path",
            "cweId": "CWE-73",
            "cweName": "External Control of File Name or Path",
            "cvssScore": 5.4,
            "offensivePriority": "P3",
            "offensivePriorityLabel": "Internal Network / Privileged Position",
            "offensivePriorityReason": "Internal Network / Privileged Position | *exposure unverified \u2014 no CMDB context; AV:N (network-routable; internet exposure unconfirmed)*",
            "confidence": 0.65,
            "description": "#### Description\nloadConfig sets result.stateDir = resolveConfiguredPath(result.stateDir || base.stateDir, result.repoPath) (config.ts:165); resolveConfiguredPath (config.ts:8-10) returns path.normalize(value) for absolute paths with no check that the result stays inside the repo. openStateDatabase (db.ts:8-14) then executes mkdir(stateDir, {recursive: true}) and new DatabaseSync(path.join(stateDir, \"factory.db\"), ...) and runs DDL (db.ts:19-78) against whatever database exists at that path. The same unconfined repoPath (config.ts:164) becomes the cwd for git operations, so the factory will 'git checkout'/'git pull --ff-only' inside any local repository an attacker names. Both values originate in factory/config.json (lines 3-4), a shared file editable through PRs. Because the DB filename is fixed, the direct primitive is: arbitrary directory creation, arbitrary factory.db creation/overwrite, and DDL execution against a pre-existing factory.db the victim keeps somewhere on disk.\n\n#### Impact\nstateDir (and repoPath) in the repo-committed factory/config.json are resolved with no confinement to the repository root, so openStateDatabase creates directories and writes/opens a SQLite database \u2014 running CREATE TABLE/ALTER TABLE DDL against it \u2014 at an attacker-chosen absolute path. This can clobber or corrupt an existing file named factory.db (plus -wal/-shm side files) in an arbitrary writable location and redirects agent worktree creation (git.ts prepareWorktree joins stateDir) to the same location.\n\n#### Exploit scenario\nAttacker's PR sets factory/config.json \"stateDir\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\dev\\\\data\\\" (or /var/backups on a shared CI host). A developer checks out the branch and runs the factory. openStateDatabase writes factory.db, factory.db-wal and factory.db-shm into the victim's data directory and runs CREATE TABLE/ALTER TABLE against any existing factory.db there, corrupting that application's state; worktrees with agent-generated code are also created under the same attacker-chosen directory.\n\n#### Preconditions\n- Attacker can open/merge a PR that modifies stateDir (or repoPath) in factory/config.json (low-privilege repo contributor)\n- A developer or CI host checks out that change and runs any factory command that opens the state database (run-once, start, doctor)\n- For corruption impact, a pre-existing factory.db must exist at the targeted path (for directory/file-creation impact, any writable location suffices)\n\n```\nconst databasePath = path.join(stateDir, \"factory.db\");\nif (!readOnly) await mkdir(stateDir, { recursive: true });\nif (readOnly && !existsSync(databasePath)) {\n  throw new Error(`Factory state database does not exist: ${databasePath}`);\n}\nconst db = new DatabaseSync(databasePath, { readOnly, timeout: 5000 });\n```\n\n#### How to fix\nConfigured paths must resolve inside the repository root. In resolveConfiguredPath (factory/src/config.ts:8-10) or immediately after it in loadConfig (config.ts:164-165), compute path.resolve and reject (with a clear validation error in validateConfig) any stateDir/repoPath that is not the base repo directory or a subdirectory of it (resolved-prefix startsWith check with a path-separator guard), so openStateDatabase (factory/src/db.ts:9-14) can only ever create the database under <repo>/tmp/AllLlmFactory.\n\n**Exploitability:** Likely CVSS 5-7-class: config-controlled stateDir and repoPath allow arbitrary directory creation, factory.db overwrite, and DDL against an attacker-named pre-existing database, plus git operations against any local repo. The immediate primitive is state corruption and arbitrary file/directory manipulation, which is more useful as a staging or persistence primitive than as a standalone RCE path unless paired with another code-execution bug.\n\n#### Adversarial verification\n**Verdict:** TRUE_POSITIVE (confidence: 9/10) \u2014 config-controlled stateDir/repoPath escape from shared config.json into arbitrary local paths; mkdir/factory.db creation + DDL against victim's pre-existing D\u2026"
          },
