            "description": "#### Description\nUntrusted input (HTTP requests from any adjacent host) enters the llama-server listener created at line 7 (`--host 0.0.0.0`) and is acted on directly: no security decision \u2014 no API key, no localhost-only bind, no client allowlist \u2014 exists anywhere between the listener and request handling. llama.cpp's OpenAI-compatible API is unauthenticated by default, and `--metrics` (line 33) is enabled, exposing model name, slot state, and perf counters to every requester. The exception in this slice proves the pattern is fixable: llm-servers/llama/windows/scripts/start-embedding.ps1:8 correctly binds 127.0.0.1. Same defect: llm-servers/llama/linux/start.sh:21, llm-servers/llama/linux/start-gemma.sh:48, llm-servers/llama/windows/NPU/scripts/start-npu.ps1:41, llm-servers/llama/windows/scripts/start-*.ps1 (all --host 0.0.0.0), llm-servers/sglang/start-qwen36-awq.sh:10, llm-servers/vllm/start.sh:1.\n\n#### Impact\nAny device on the developer's LAN can issue inference requests to the model without credentials, exhausting GPU/VRAM and starving the developer's own single-slot (--parallel 1) workloads, and can read model, slot, and performance telemetry from the unauthenticated /metrics endpoint. The identical bind appears in roughly 15 other launch scripts across beellama, llama/windows, llama/linux, sglang, and vllm.\n\n#### Exploit scenario\nA LAN neighbor runs `curl -s -X POST http://<devhost>:8080/v1/chat/completions -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"model\":\"local\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"hi\"}],\"max_tokens\":4096}'` and receives a completion with no 401. Repeating with long prompts against the single parallel slot starves the developer's inference workloads, and `curl http://<devhost>:8080/metrics` discloses the loaded model name and slot/perf state.\n\n#### Preconditions\n- attacker is on the same network segment as the developer host\n- one of the start-*.ps1 / start*.sh servers is running\n\n```\n& $exe `\n  -m $model `\n  --host 0.0.0.0 `\n  --port 8080 `\n  --gpu-layers all `\n  ...\n  --metrics `\n  --slots\n```\n\n#### How to fix\nLocal inference endpoints must not be reachable without authentication outside the host: change `--host 0.0.0.0` to `--host 127.0.0.1` in every launch script (beellama/scripts/start-*.ps1, llama/windows/scripts/start-*.ps1, llama/windows/NPU/scripts/start-npu.ps1, llama/linux/start.sh, llama/linux/start-gemma.sh, sglang/start-qwen36-awq.sh line 10, vllm/start.sh), matching start-embedding.ps1:8; if genuine LAN access is required, terminate it through an authenticating reverse proxy instead of binding 0.0.0.0.\n\n**Exploitability:** Likely CVSS 4-6-class: llama-server is bound to all interfaces with no authentication, leaking prompts/model state and enabling inference DoS. The primitive is confidentiality/availability impact rather than direct code execution. It is valuable in chains because it can expose local inference traffic, model names, or prompt data to adjacent actors.\n\n#### Adversarial verification\n**Verdict:** TRUE_POSITIVE (confidence: 8/10) \u2014 0.0.0.0:8080 llama/vllm/sglang servers with no API key/auth and --metrics enabled are reachable unauthenticated from the same network segment (confirmed across all start scripts; only the embedding script binds 127.0.0.1), giving LAN neighbors model access, metrics disclosure, and single-slot GPU exhaustion \u2014 a real but low-impact misconfig, kept per the boundary-crossing exception."
          },
